# Security headers for static and prerendered responses. Cloudflare's assets
# layer applies this file; the adapter appends its own autogenerated cache and
# X-Robots-Tag block below at build time, so do not add rules for /_app/* here.
#
# Lives at the project root, not in static/ — adapter-cloudflare hard-errors on
# a _headers file under the assets directory.
#
# This file does NOT cover server-rendered routes (/d/<key>, /dashboard, the API
# proxy) — those responses never pass through the assets layer. The same headers
# are set for them in src/hooks.server.ts. Keep the two lists identical.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy: SvelteKit hydration emits an inline <script> on
# every page, so a CSP without unsafe-inline would break hydration. Doing it
# properly needs SvelteKit's csp config to emit nonces or hashes. Separate job.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
